MSI-Net saliency model (used by the attention check; downloaded on first use,
not stored in this repository)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File:    msi-net-salicon-d950b35.onnx  (50,041,285 bytes)
SHA-256: 9a6d3605dff7846ecc8e180031787d8152d5269773db869aa11c21eb0b59cb0f
Hosted:  https://github.com/simonlunay/redline/releases/tag/saliency-msi-net-v1

Source:  "Contextual encoder-decoder network for visual saliency prediction",
         Kroner, Senden, Driessens, Goebel, Neural Networks 129 (2020) 261-270.
         Weights: https://huggingface.co/alexanderkroner/MSI-Net
         at commit d950b35945db961ae63f84bc2b23f6bd578d0b8f (SALICON-trained model).
         Code:    https://github.com/alexanderkroner/saliency

Modifications: converted from the TensorFlow SavedModel to ONNX (opset 17) with
tf2onnx 1.16.1, then to float16 weights with onnxconverter-common (float32 inputs
and outputs kept). The output matches the original within 0.0007 (on a 0-1 scale).
Conversion script: packages/checker/scripts/convert-msi-net.py

