Training-data caveats (not legal advice; get a legal review before any
commercial use):
- The weights were trained on SALICON (mouse-tracking "attention" annotations
  on MS COCO images). I could not confirm the SALICON annotation license on
  the official site (salicon.net); secondary sources describe it as CC BY 4.0.
  The underlying COCO images come from Flickr under a mix of per-image licenses.
- The encoder was initialized from VGG16 weights pretrained on ImageNet, whose
  image terms of access are for non-commercial research. How such terms apply
  to models derived from those weights is legally unsettled.
- The model predicts attention on natural photos; it was not trained on
  graphic designs, and its output is a prediction, not measured eye tracking.

